   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The model is \\( \\frac{dB}{dt} = kB \\). Separating and integrating gives \\( \\ln|B| = kt + C \\), so \\( B = B_0 e^{kt} \\), and the value at t = 0 gives \\( B_0 = 380 \\).",
         "rule_named": "separation of variables for proportional growth"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The second value gives \\( 152 = 380 e^{1k} \\), so \\( k = \\ln{\\left(\\frac{2}{5} \\right)} \\).",
         "rule_named": "constant from a second data pair"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Therefore \\( B(t) = 380 e^{t \\ln{\\left(\\frac{2}{5} \\right)}} \\) bacteria.",
